        <item>
            <title>1.16.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 02:10:00 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.16.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.16.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h3>Vox gives you your disk space back</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Vox reclaims space that earlier versions left behind. When Vox starts, it removes duplicate copies of models that no loader reads. On a Mac that used earlier versions this can free hundreds of megabytes. Vox never removes a model you use.</li>
                    <li>Deleting a model now removes every copy of it. Before this, Vox kept two cached copies, so you got back about one third of the space Vox told you it freed.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>More control in the Storage tab</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Clear your recordings, your voice previews, and partial downloads. Vox asks you to confirm before it removes recordings, because Vox cannot recreate them. The text stays in History.</li>
                    <li>Every row has a Reveal in Finder button.</li>
                    <li>The Listening tab lists the speech models you downloaded, with the real size of each one and a Remove button.</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
            <enclosure
                url="https://github.com/gregbarbosa/vox-appcast/releases/download/v1.16.0/Vox-1.16.0.zip"
