        <item>
            <title>1.12.0</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 17:45:13 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.12.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.12.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h3>New</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Rewrite styles for dictation.</strong> Just talk — Vox now cleans up what you said. It drops filler words (“um”, “you know”), tidies false starts, and applies your self-corrections (“Tuesday — no, Wednesday” becomes “Wednesday”). Pick how it shapes the result: <em>Clean</em> to just neaten it up, or <em>Email</em>, <em>Message</em>, <em>Notes</em>, and <em>Prose</em> to format for where it’s going — or keep <em>Verbatim</em> (the default) for exactly what you said. It runs on-device with Apple Intelligence, so nothing leaves your Mac. Choose a style in Settings → Listening, or from the new wand button on the recording pill.</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
