        <item>
            <title>1.9.3</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 30 Jun 2026 19:44:00 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.9.3</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.9.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h3>New</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Long passages now read all the way through.</strong> Selections that used to fail with “Synthesis failed” are split into natural chunks and start playing while the rest is still being prepared, so audio begins almost immediately.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Fixed</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Reading aloud in Safari no longer disturbs your clipboard.</strong> Vox now captures your Safari selection directly, even on the very first try, instead of falling back to copy-and-paste.</li>
                    <li><strong>Closing the player mid-synthesis makes it stay closed.</strong> The floating player no longer pops back open (or shows a raw model name) when you dismiss it while a long passage is still being prepared.</li>
                    <li><strong>A calmer launch.</strong> Vox no longer force-opens System Settings on startup — it shows a gentle menu-bar prompt and only opens Settings when you ask to grant access.</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
