        <item>
            <title>1.8.7</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 29 Jun 2026 19:44:53 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.8.7</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.8.7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h3>Fixed</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Crash on rapid hotkey presses.</strong> Pressing the speak hotkey again while Vox was still working could crash the app. A new press now cleanly interrupts and replaces the one in progress.</li>
                    <li><strong>More reliable text capture.</strong> Selected-text capture is more robust in browsers and other apps, with a smarter clipboard fallback that no longer reads stale or unrelated clipboard content when nothing is selected.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Improved</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Faster, more accurate transcript cleanup.</strong> The Fast “Clean up transcript” tier downloads and runs an on-device punctuation model on first use, with an instant rule-based fallback so it never blocks.</li>
                    <li><strong>Dictation download progress.</strong> The Parakeet dictation model now shows a real progress bar with a working Cancel button in Settings → Listening.</li>
                    <li><strong>Capture diagnostics.</strong> Settings → Debug now shows exactly why a capture succeeded or failed (per-strategy results and timings).</li>
                    <li><strong>AirPods audio quality.</strong> Opening Settings no longer holds the microphone open, so Bluetooth output stays at full quality.</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
